      "writtenOn": "2024-09-11T02:34:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the reading and comments!\n\n\u003eQuerying stuff after transforms is actually something that the Tint team wants to remove over time, it just hasn\u0027t done it for HLSL yet.\n\nThat\u0027s a big change. Still possible to achieve \"use exact numbers of immediate data slots\". Tint Reflection might provide enough infos (as you mentioned in below comments about useVertexIndex). But I\u0027m not sure whether some transforms e.g. \"ArrayLengthFromUniform\" (https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/tint/lang/wgsl/ast/transform/array_length_from_uniform.cc;drc\u003da6941c6ee100b201f6f02c12e90fa8c05c3a607f;l\u003d261) (which only emit (from 0 to) highest dynamic storage buffer(analysis in trasforms) size variables) might generate builtins or additional codes which uses part of immediate datas. \nTo be clear about the concern, take \"vertex index offset\" as an example, tint reflection told us no vertexIndex or instance index has been used, but after applying some hlsl specific transforms, some generated code uses them. So we got false info from tint reflection. \n\nBut it might be Ok. API side could know the final result by query proper tint reflection info combined with API side toggle/workaround/extra command utils info.\n\nBut still need your wise about this.\n\n\n\n\n\u003eLet me know if you\u0027d like a small meeting to discuss all of this, I know it\u0027s a lot but a clear solution is in sight!\n\nThanks! That would be great! Pls send me the calendar after you find the available time slot!",
      "parentUuid": "c84c6c07_235e82d5",
      "revId": "1392ccb155b29453b7f1c581eb4f814d7ca830c0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
