      "writtenOn": "2024-09-11T14:19:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you know when the HLSL translation adds uses of useVertexIndex / useInstanceIndex? My understanding is that we only need to add the variables when the FirstIndexOffset transforms does something useful so we should be good?\n\nWe pass information in random places in the D3D12 backend but for all of arglengths, firstIndexOffset and NumWorkgroup we pass binding points to Tint. Right now these have to be different bindings points because Tint will generate different ConstantBuffer\u003c\u003e for each, but Dawn can still compute them as a single bunch of root constants except that ah ... but then the root signature depends on them instead of only the total immediate size.\n\nOk so we have a chicken and egg problem where we need to move these transforms to use immediates when we don\u0027t have support for them yet in the D3D12 backend.\n\nSo let\u0027s do things in this order:\n\n - Add some skeleton support of immediates in the D3D12 backend (still with full dirty bits, caching of root signature etc), and use it for arglength only.\n - Move Tint to allow use of var\u003cimmediate\u003e for argLength (as an option) and make the HLSL option take a register space + register number for the immediates, as well as an offset for where the arglength should be.\n - Move Tint to allow use of immediate for numworkgroups, make the D3D12 backend use that.\n - Move Tint to allow use of immediate for vertex/index, use it in D3D12 backend.\n - Add support for immediates in WGSL, plump it in the frontend API, have it all work in D3D12.\n - Remove options to use non-immediates for the various Tint transforms.",
      "parentUuid": "b7f33686_c73095fb",
      "revId": "1392ccb155b29453b7f1c581eb4f814d7ca830c0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
