      "writtenOn": "2024-09-10T08:30:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking forward to the formal comments:P\n\nDirty bit is a good idea but I debated in my mind about two uploading model many times:\n - Multiple CPU calls to upload several dirty pieces. Don\u0027t waste any bandwidth but\n   start uploading process many times \n - Single CPU calls to upload continuous range with non-necessary flush. Waste bandwidth but start uploading process only once.\n \nMaybe a high-low dirty range is a balanced way?\n\n\u003e   SetNumWorkgroups(x, y, z);\n   SetBufferLength();\n\nUsing function name instead of enum is a great idea!\n\nIf we have new \"RootSignature\" object, I\u0027d like to put this immediate data block struct/class in RootSignatureBase.",
      "parentUuid": "d7992395_a3666bb3",
      "revId": "1392ccb155b29453b7f1c581eb4f814d7ca830c0",
