        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-09T16:51:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This looks good overall, but I think we can do better with a map\u003ckey, Ref\u003cRootSignature\u003e\u003e with RootSignature being our new object that contains info about the D3D12 root signature. Then store a ref to that in the pipeline directly instead of querying with the rangeSizes over and over again.\n\nThat said the root signature itself only depends on how many u32s we need, not what we put in them. So maybe a mix of option 1 and 2, with the pipeline layout keeping a cache of root signature with varying numbers of constants, but the pipeline themselves knowing where to put each constant? But also the pipeline layout could keep other caches like GetDispatchWithNumWG(total constant size, wgOffset).",
      "revId": "1392ccb155b29453b7f1c581eb4f814d7ca830c0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
